msgid "How to interpret the shaded lightcone visualizations for the latest version of Shaded lightcones"
msgstr "Cara menginterpretasikan visualisasi shaded lightcone untuk versi terbaru Shaded lightcones"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "How to interpret the shaded lightcone visualizations"
msgstr "Cara menginterpretasikan visualisasi shaded lightcone"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<OpenInLabBanner notebookPath=\"addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/interpreting-visualizations.ipynb\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The package provides two ways to look at a shaded lightcone:\n"
msgstr "Paket ini menyediakan dua cara untuk melihat shaded lightcone:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`draw_shaded_lightcone` overlays the bounds onto the circuit diagram. THis is best for circuits on a 1D\n"
"chain of qubits, where the circuit diagram and the physical layout agree.\n"
msgstr ""
"`draw_shaded_lightcone` menumpangkan bound ke diagram circuit. Ini paling cocok untuk circuit pada rantai qubit 1D,\n"
"di mana diagram circuit dan layout fisik sejalan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`animate_shaded_lightcone` projects the bounds onto the QPU's coupling map and steps through the\n"
"circuit layer by layer. This is best when the qubit connectivity is more than a 1D line, where a circuit\n"
"diagram stops conveying which qubits are neighbors.\n"
msgstr ""
"`animate_shaded_lightcone` memproyeksikan bound ke coupling map QPU dan melangkah melalui\n"
"circuit layer demi layer. Ini paling cocok ketika konektivitas qubit lebih dari garis 1D, di mana diagram\n"
"circuit tidak lagi menunjukkan qubit mana yang bertetangga.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Both visualizations show the same underlying numbers. This guide covers what those numbers mean, and explains the details\n"
"that are easy to misread.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kedua visualisasi menampilkan angka dasar yang sama. Panduan ini membahas arti angka-angka itu, dan menjelaskan detail\n"
"yang gampang salah dibaca.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Penyiapan {#setup}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the same Trotterized Ising circuit and observable as the [quickstart guide](/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/quickstart).\n"
msgstr "Pakai circuit Ising hasil Trotterisasi dan observable yang sama dengan [panduan quickstart](/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/quickstart).\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "`draw_shaded_lightcone` {#draw-shaded-lightcone}"
msgstr "`draw_shaded_lightcone` {#draw-shaded-lightcone}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Each noisy box is shaded by the bound on the errors occurring there: bright means a large bound, and\n"
"a box fading into the background means its errors have little effect on the observable. Those faded\n"
"boxes are the candidates for dropping from the mitigated noise model.\n"
msgstr ""
"Setiap box yang noisy diberi bayangan sesuai bound error yang terjadi di sana: terang berarti bound besar, dan\n"
"box yang memudar ke latar berarti error-nya berpengaruh kecil pada observable. Box yang memudar itu\n"
"adalah kandidat untuk dibuang dari model noise yang dimitigasi.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/interpreting-visualizations/extracted-outputs/cell-04-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/interpreting-visualizations/extracted-outputs/cell-04-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Important notes {#important-notes}"
msgstr "Catatan penting {#important-notes}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**1. Each number is a sum over the error terms sharing a support.** Without a filter, the bounds of\n"
"every error term acting on the same qubit, or on the same pair of qubits, are added into one value:\n"
"all three Pauli types on a qubit, and all nine on a pair. That has two consequences. A value can\n"
"exceed 2.0, even though no single term's bound can (a box labelled `4.5` is several terms adding up,\n"
"not a violated bound). The figure cannot tell you whether a large value comes from one Pauli\n"
"type or from several comparable ones; the next section shows how to separate them.\n"
msgstr ""
"**1. Setiap angka adalah jumlah dari suku error yang berbagi support yang sama.** Tanpa filter, bound dari\n"
"setiap suku error yang bekerja pada qubit yang sama, atau pada pasangan qubit yang sama, dijumlahkan menjadi satu nilai:\n"
"ketiga tipe Pauli pada satu qubit, dan kesembilannya pada sepasang qubit. Ini punya dua konsekuensi. Sebuah nilai bisa\n"
"melebihi 2.0, padahal bound satu suku saja tidak mungkin (box berlabel `4.5` adalah beberapa suku yang dijumlahkan,\n"
"bukan bound yang dilanggar). Gambarnya juga tidak bisa memberi tahu apakah nilai besar berasal dari satu tipe\n"
"Pauli atau dari beberapa yang sebanding; bagian berikutnya menunjukkan cara memisahkannya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**2. The color scale starts at 2.0 and grows with the data.** The scale runs from 0 to the\n"
"`\"max_bound\"` entry of the overlaid circuit's metadata, which is the larger of 2.0 and the largest\n"
"value shown. Unfiltered sums often exceed 2.0, so the scale stretches to fit them, and the same\n"
"color can stand for different values in different figures. When every value is small, the\n"
"scale stays at 2.0 and everything looks uniformly dark (that is the scale reflecting the absolute\n"
"size, not a rendering fault).\n"
msgstr ""
"**2. Skala warna dimulai dari 2.0 dan tumbuh mengikuti data.** Skalanya berjalan dari 0 sampai entri\n"
"`\"max_bound\"` di metadata circuit yang ditumpangi, yaitu yang lebih besar antara 2.0 dan nilai\n"
"terbesar yang ditampilkan. Jumlah tanpa filter sering melebihi 2.0, jadi skala melebar untuk menampungnya, dan warna\n"
"yang sama bisa mewakili nilai berbeda di gambar yang berbeda. Ketika semua nilai kecil,\n"
"skala tetap di 2.0 dan semuanya tampak gelap seragam (itu skala yang mencerminkan ukuran\n"
"absolut, bukan kesalahan render).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Separating the Pauli types {#separating-the-pauli-types}"
msgstr "Memisahkan tipe Pauli {#separating-the-pauli-types}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Use `pauli_filter` to see one type at a time. An integer selects a Pauli weight; a string selects\n"
"a specific Pauli, matched against each noise term **reduced to its own non-identity support**. So\n"
"`\"X\"` selects every single-qubit $X$ error, regardless of which qubit it acts on, and `\"XX\"` selects the\n"
"weight-2 ones (a full-width label like `\"XII\"` matches nothing).\n"
msgstr ""
"Pakai `pauli_filter` untuk melihat satu tipe pada satu waktu. Bilangan bulat memilih bobot Pauli; string memilih\n"
"Pauli tertentu, yang dicocokkan dengan setiap suku noise **yang direduksi ke support non-identity miliknya sendiri**. Jadi\n"
"`\"X\"` memilih setiap error $X$ satu-qubit, apa pun qubit tempatnya bekerja, dan `\"XX\"` memilih yang\n"
"berbobot 2 (label selebar penuh seperti `\"XII\"` tidak cocok dengan apa pun).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The unfiltered row is the sum of the three Pauli types below it. Filtering is the only way to tell\n"
"whether a large unfiltered value comes from one dominant error type or from several comparable ones.\n"
"That matters, because the mitigation acts per term, not per site.\n"
msgstr ""
"Baris tanpa filter adalah jumlah dari ketiga tipe Pauli di bawahnya. Memfilter adalah satu-satunya cara untuk mengetahui\n"
"apakah nilai besar tanpa filter berasal dari satu tipe error yang dominan atau dari beberapa yang sebanding.\n"
"Itu penting, karena mitigasi bekerja per suku, bukan per site.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Passing the same filter to `draw_shaded_lightcone` records it in the figure title, so a filtered\n"
"figure cannot be mistaken for an unfiltered one:\n"
msgstr ""
"Memberikan filter yang sama ke `draw_shaded_lightcone` mencatatnya di judul gambar, sehingga gambar\n"
"yang difilter tidak bisa tertukar dengan yang tanpa filter:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/interpreting-visualizations/extracted-outputs/cell-09-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/interpreting-visualizations/extracted-outputs/cell-09-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This figure looks quite different from the unfiltered one above, and not only because it shows\n"
"fewer values. Each placeholder in these figures stands for one support: a single qubit, or a pair of\n"
"qubits. Without a filter, a box shows a placeholder on every qubit and on every pair of neighboring\n"
"qubits, so it spreads over several columns. With `\"X\"`, only the single-qubit supports remain, and\n"
"each box shrinks to a single column.\n"
msgstr ""
"Gambar ini tampak cukup berbeda dari yang tanpa filter di atas, dan bukan hanya karena menampilkan\n"
"lebih sedikit nilai. Setiap placeholder di gambar-gambar ini mewakili satu support: satu qubit, atau sepasang\n"
"qubit. Tanpa filter, sebuah box menampilkan placeholder di setiap qubit dan di setiap pasangan qubit\n"
"bertetangga, jadi ia melebar ke beberapa kolom. Dengan `\"X\"`, hanya support satu-qubit yang tersisa, dan\n"
"setiap box menyusut menjadi satu kolom.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Neither picture shows what PEC actually applies though. The placeholders are a way to display\n"
"bounds, not anti-noise gates. During the experiment, every box whose error terms are mitigated is\n"
"treated as a single layer of two-qubit gates, and the anti-noise Paulis sampled for its error terms\n"
"are composed into one Pauli that is applied to that layer as a whole.\n"
msgstr "Tapi kedua gambar itu tidak menunjukkan apa yang sebenarnya diterapkan PEC. Placeholder-nya hanyalah cara untuk menampilkan batas (bound), bukan gate anti-noise. Selama eksperimen, setiap kotak yang suku error-nya dimitigasi diperlakukan sebagai satu layer gate dua qubit, dan Pauli anti-noise yang disampel untuk suku error-nya digabung menjadi satu Pauli yang diterapkan ke layer tersebut secara keseluruhan.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "`animate_shaded_lightcone` {#animate-shaded-lightcone}"
msgstr "`animate_shaded_lightcone` {#animate-shaded-lightcone}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"On a device whose connectivity is not a 1D line, a circuit diagram no longer shows which qubits are\n"
"neighbors, so the spatial spread of the lightcone becomes impossible to read.\n"
"`animate_shaded_lightcone` instead draws the QPU's coupling map and animates the bounds across it,\n"
"one noisy box per frame.\n"
msgstr "Pada perangkat yang konektivitasnya bukan garis 1D, diagram circuit tidak lagi menunjukkan qubit mana yang bertetangga, sehingga sebaran spasial lightcone jadi mustahil dibaca. `animate_shaded_lightcone` justru menggambar coupling map QPU dan menganimasikan bound di atasnya, satu kotak berisik (noisy box) per frame.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It needs a `CouplingMap`, which it lays out on a grid by embedding the device graph, so it handles both\n"
"heavy-hex and square connectivity.\n"
msgstr "Fungsi ini membutuhkan `CouplingMap`, yang ditata di atas grid dengan cara menanamkan graf perangkat, sehingga bisa menangani konektivitas heavy-hex maupun persegi.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<div class=\"alert alert-info\">\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Note:** In this rendered documentation the animation is static. The slider and play button only\n"
"work when the notebook runs interactively, for example in Jupyter.\n"
msgstr "**Catatan:** Di dokumentasi yang sudah dirender ini, animasinya statis. Slider dan tombol play hanya berfungsi saat notebook dijalankan secara interaktif, misalnya di Jupyter.\n"

